// Two INDEPENDENT existentials (distinct bound vars `u` and `v`, no join)
// — contrast with ea_0012, which shares one `u` across both predicates.
// "Some login AND some transfer happened in the window", even by DIFFERENT
// users. The point: a login by alice and a transfer by bob suffices here,
// whereas the shared-var correlation would require the same user to do both.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (u: String). formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: u } && exists (v: String). formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: v }};
